text:
jun: Heads-up: sampleapp CI failing on embed+rerank parity between Node & Python. Node SDK's batching helper returns nested arrays for single inputs sometimes; Python returns a flat vector. Also saw rerank response use 'ranking_score' instead of 'score' in hosted API, which breaks our client mapping. Auth retries seem to exacerbate (duplicate calls). Logs + snippets below.

maya: Can you paste minimal repro?

jun: Sure, pared down repro. Node batching helper output vs python and a rerank response sample:

```
POST /v1/embeddings
Body:
{ "input": ["a short query"], "model": "open-embedding-1536" }

// Node (what sampleapp helper produces)
const batch = batchingHelper([{ text: "a short query" }]);
console.log(batch.length) // 1
console.log(Array.isArray(batch[0])) // true  // <-- nested vector
// Server returns:
{ "data": [[0.001, 0.002, /* ... 1536 values ... */]] }

// Python client returns:
{ "data": [0.001, 0.002, /* ... 1536 values ... */] }

// Rerank response we saw from hosted API:
{ "results": [ { "id": "a", "ranking_score": 0.812 } ] }
// Our client code expects `score` and breaks.

// Extra: node auth middleware retries on 401 and resends without preserving generated id headers, so server processes request twice in some cases.
```

sam: I can reproduce the nested-array behavior. Looks like the helper does `return inputs.map(batchify)` and when batchify returns an array we end up with double nesting for single-item batches. Quick fix is to flatten when batchSize === 1. I'll open a small PR.

igor: Re: auth retry — this matches an open bug: node-auth v0.5 retries on 401 but doesn't keep the original x-request-id/idempotency token. Server can't dedupe, so you get two processed requests. Mitigation: attach a client-generated `x-rw-idempotency-token` and retain it across retries, or make retry only refresh token without re-sending the body. I'll file DEVEX ticket.

olivia: Workaround for the sampleapp until fixes land: normalize embeddings shape and map fallback scores on the client side. Example snippet:

```js
// normalize embedding shape
let embeddings = response.data;
if (!Array.isArray(embeddings[0])) {
  embeddings = [embeddings];
}

// map rerank score fallback
const mapped = results.map(r => ({
  id: r.id,
  score: r.score ?? r.ranking_score ?? r.confidence
}));
```

Works for both SDKs and both naming conventions. :thumbsup:

devex-bot: Created issue DEVEX-2487 tracking: "node batching helper returns nested arrays for single-item batches + preserve idempotency token across auth retries". Linking PRs: prs/6789 (node helper fix) and prs/6790 (auth retry fix). Added e2e tests request.

maya: Great. Can we add an e2e test in sampleapp that asserts both SDKs return identical normalized shape and mapped rerank score? If yes, add to PR and ping me for review.

jun: Will add tests to sampleapp and include the workaround mapping in the short-term patch. Thanks all.
